# semgrep ignore list (gitignore syntax).
#
# frontend/ is the React reference portal. semgrep's default JS/TS rules flag
# jsx-not-internationalized on every user-facing string (~60 findings) and a
# few style rules (package version ranges, JSON.stringify keys). This sample
# intentionally ships a single-language demo UI — internationalization is out
# of scope for a reference implementation — so the portal is excluded from
# semgrep. Security-relevant logic lives in the backend control plane and the
# runtime kernels, which are still scanned.
frontend/

# Test code. The adversarial suites deliberately build hostile inputs: fake
# credentials, shell commands assembled from variables, sleeps that race a
# timeout, unauthenticated cipher modes to forge payloads. semgrep's audit rules
# fire on exactly those patterns, so test files produced most of the findings
# and none of them were defects. Production code under backend/, runtimes/,
# services/, scripts/ and terraform/ is still scanned; the few by-design hits
# there carry an inline `nosemgrep: <rule>  (reason)`.
tests/
test_*.py
*_adversarial.py

# Standard build / dependency output (not committed, listed for completeness).
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.git/
cdk.out/
